// ============================================================================
// EXAMPLE: @define and @use for Reusable Legal Blocks
// ============================================================================
// This document demonstrates how @define stores named blocks (without rendering)
// and @use inserts them at specific locations. No parameters, conditionals, or
// loops are used - just simple block substitution.
// ============================================================================

@meta
  date: March 15, 2026
  parties:
    landlord: RIVERSIDE PROPERTIES, LLC
    tenant: JAMES & MARIA CHEN

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DEFINITIONS: These blocks are stored but NOT rendered here
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@define notice_clause
  **NOTICE.** All notices under this Agreement shall be in writing and shall 
  be deemed given when: (a) delivered personally; (b) sent by certified mail, 
  return receipt requested; or (c) sent by overnight courier, to the addresses 
  set forth below or to such other address as a party may designate in writing.

  @indent
    If to Landlord:
    {{parties.landlord}}
    Attn: Property Manager
    123 Main Street, Suite 400
    Minneapolis, MN 55401

    If to Tenant:
    {{parties.tenant}}
    [Property Address]
  @;

@define signature_block_landlord
  **LANDLORD:**

  {{parties.landlord}}


  By: ________________________________
      Name: ___________________________
      Its: Authorized Representative

  Date: ______________________________

@define signature_block_tenant
  **TENANT:**


  ________________________________
  {{parties.tenant}}

  Date: ______________________________

@define governing_law
  **GOVERNING LAW.** This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in 
  accordance with the laws of the State of Minnesota, without regard to 
  conflict of laws principles. Any dispute arising under this Agreement 
  shall be resolved in the courts of Hennepin County, Minnesota.

@define standard_recitals
  **WHEREAS**, Landlord is the owner of the Property described in [[Exhibit A]]; and

  **WHEREAS**, Tenant desires to lease the Property from Landlord for the 
  purposes described herein; and

  **WHEREAS**, Landlord desires to lease the Property to Tenant on the terms 
  and conditions set forth in this Agreement;

  **NOW, THEREFORE**, in consideration of the mutual covenants contained herein 
  and for other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of 
  which are hereby acknowledged, the parties agree as follows:

// ============================================================================
// MAIN DOCUMENT: The Agreement
// ============================================================================

@center
  # COMMERCIAL LEASE AGREEMENT

THIS COMMERCIAL LEASE AGREEMENT ("Agreement") is made and entered into as of 
{{date}}, by and between {{parties.landlord}} ("Landlord") and 
{{parties.tenant}} ("Tenant").

## Recitals

@use standard_recitals

## Agreement

@anchor Article 1
@1 Premises.
Landlord hereby leases to Tenant, and Tenant hereby leases from Landlord, the 
premises described in [[Exhibit A]] (the "Premises"), subject to the terms and 
conditions of this Agreement.

@anchor Article 2
@2 Term.
The initial term of this Lease shall be for a period of five (5) years, 
commencing on May 1, 2026 and ending on April 30, 2031, unless sooner 
terminated in accordance with the provisions hereof.

@anchor Article 3
@3 Rent.

@@a **Base Rent.** Tenant shall pay to Landlord base rent in the amount of 
FIVE THOUSAND DOLLARS ($5,000.00) per month, due on the first day of each month.

@@b **Late Fee.** If any rent payment is not received within five (5) days of 
the due date, Tenant shall pay a late fee equal to five percent (5%) of the 
overdue amount.

@anchor Article 4
@4 Notices.

@use notice_clause

@anchor Article 5
@5 Miscellaneous.

@@a **Entire Agreement.** This Agreement, together with the Exhibits attached 
hereto, constitutes the entire agreement between the parties with respect to 
the subject matter hereof.

@@b @use governing_law

@@c **Amendments.** This Agreement may not be amended or modified except by a 
written instrument signed by both parties.

**IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, the parties have executed this Agreement as of the date 
first written above.

@use signature_block_landlord

@use signature_block_tenant


@pagebreak

// ============================================================================
// EXHIBIT A: Property Description
// ============================================================================

@center
  # EXHIBIT A
  
  Legal Description of the Premises

@anchor Exhibit A
The Premises consists of approximately 2,500 square feet of commercial space 
located at:

@box
  **Property Address:**
  456 Commerce Boulevard, Suite 200
  Minneapolis, MN 55402
  
  **Legal Description:**
  Lot 12, Block 3, Commerce Park Addition
  Hennepin County, Minnesota
@;

The Premises includes access to common areas, parking (4 designated spaces), 
and building amenities as described in the Building Rules attached hereto.


@pagebreak

// ============================================================================
// EXHIBIT B: Additional Lease Terms
// ============================================================================

@center
  # EXHIBIT B
  
  Additional Terms and Conditions

@anchor Exhibit B

@1 Insurance Requirements.
Tenant shall maintain commercial general liability insurance with minimum 
coverage of ONE MILLION DOLLARS ($1,000,000) per occurrence.

@2 Permitted Use.
The Premises shall be used solely for general office purposes and such other 
lawful purposes as may be approved in writing by Landlord.

@3 Notice Requirements.

// Reusing the same notice clause for consistency across exhibits
@use notice_clause


@pagebreak

// ============================================================================
// EXHIBIT C: Signature Addendum (Multi-party scenario)
// ============================================================================

@center
  # EXHIBIT C
  
  Guaranty of Lease

@anchor Exhibit C

The undersigned Guarantor(s), in consideration of the execution of the foregoing 
Lease by Landlord, hereby unconditionally guarantee to Landlord the full and 
prompt payment and performance of all obligations of Tenant under the Lease.

## Notices to Guarantor

All notices to Guarantor shall be sent in accordance with the notice provisions 
of the Agreement:

@use notice_clause

## Governing Law

@use governing_law

